# Committed, non-secret production defaults.
#
# Read this before adding anything here.
#
# Next.js loads this file for production builds AND in the production runtime,
# and a value present here can win over the one configured in Vercel. That makes
# it the wrong place for a placeholder.
#
# This file used to carry placeholder database, NextAuth, Google OAuth and
# Nutrient credentials, added to avoid "Invalid URL" errors during builds. A
# placeholder connection string here can be read in preference to the real Neon
# URL configured in Vercel, which is reason enough not to keep one.
#
# They were also unnecessary: lib/prisma.ts builds its client lazily through a
# Proxy, so nothing connects to a database during the build.
#
# What these placeholders did NOT cause is the production outage that is easy to
# blame on them. Every query failing against 127.0.0.1:5432 was a separate bug —
# the Prisma adapter was handed a `pg.Pool` it could not recognise under pnpm and
# died at protocol startup, reporting a host that was never involved. That is
# explained at length in lib/prisma.ts. Both faults pointed at localhost, which
# is precisely why they were mistaken for one.
#
# Rule: only add a value here if it is not a secret AND it is correct in
# production. Anything else belongs in Vercel's environment settings alone.

# Nutrient Viewer CDN version. Not a secret, and this is the real value, so it is
# safe for it to win. Loaded by app/layout.tsx from
# https://cdn.cloud.pspdfkit.com/pspdfkit-web@<version>/nutrient-viewer.js
NUTRIENT_VIEWER_VERSION="1.20.0"

# Twilio SMS notifications. TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID and TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN are secrets
# and are deliberately left empty here — set them in Vercel's environment
# settings, not in this file. TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN also doubles as the inbound
# webhook signing key, so rotating it must happen alongside re-verifying
# app/api/webhooks/twilio/route.ts still receives messages.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=

# The program's phone number. Not a secret — it is published at
# https://jonaddams.com/sms and filed with the A2P 10DLC campaign — so the real
# value belongs here, and having it win over Vercel is the point: the Vercel
# value is encrypted and cannot be read back to confirm it is right.
#
# This must stay in step with three other places, because a carrier reviewer
# compares them: the number published on /sms, the number filed with the
# campaign, and the number the app displays on its opt-in screen. That screen
# renders this value through formatProgramNumber(), so a stale value here tells
# a user to text a number that cannot receive, and lib/twilio.ts sends every
# outbound message from it.
#
# It held the trial number +17372583742 until 2026-09-03. That number died when
# the account was upgraded; do not reintroduce it.
TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=+12692925337

# Only needed when the URL Twilio was configured to POST to differs from what
# the app sees as request.url — e.g. behind a proxy or a rewritten host. Twilio
# signs the URL it was configured with, not the one the request arrives on, so
# a mismatch here breaks inbound signature verification. Leave unset unless
# that mismatch is confirmed.
TWILIO_WEBHOOK_URL=
